>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Manually reviewed Lewis representation. The NHC, two NMe₂ groups and three CO ligands of the reported tricarbonyl diboron complex 3a match the input. The authors observed Fe–B–B backbonding and shortening of B–C. The graph uses the closed-shell C=B⁻–B=N⁺ limiting form. The B–B connection is retained. A B=B representation is related by delocalization; Low coordination at B is insufficient to assign a diradical. Localized 12 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. The atom order and coordinates of all 76 atoms agree between XYZ and SDF. Lengths of 74 nonmetal covalent bonds: 67 within range, 0 outside range and 7 with sparse controls. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

