>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Single-point calculation on the original coordinates and ligand-by-ligand Lewis review. Each of the two C₅HS₂ fragments contains two acute-angled C–C–S three-membered rings. Both bond-order analyses indicate bonding at all four terminal S–C contacts. Assign Ni(II) and two equivalent monoanions; Two terminal C⁻ atoms and a central CH⁺ give one symmetric charge-delocalization limit for each fragment. The complete electronic state is recorded separately. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

